// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 11-initialization
// facility: rule.init.definite-assignment [Definite-Assignment-Rejected] (CHG-0438): a borrow of a binding with no value; conf.borrow-of-uninitialized
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.use-of-uninitialized (static)
//
// A borrow is a use: nothing written through `r` would give `x` a value,
// and a read through it would read none.

import std;

fn main()
{
    i32 x;
    ref<i32, shared> r = &x;
    printf("%v\n", *r);
}
